            "type": "p",
            "text": "Some component-level research is also relevant to the metabolic conversation. For L-carnitine, meta-analyses of supplementation trials in adults report small average body-weight differences against control. One found about 1.3 kg (Pooyandjoo et al., 2016), and another about 1.2 kg, which its authors called modest (Talenezhad et al., 2020). Early animal work on choline examined liver fat under specific dietary conditions (Best and Ridout, 1933)."
